After a side message from Rast, I've added a new section near the top
on what you should NOT do. Is this clear and have I left anything out?

What you MUST NOT Do
====================

You will lose the game without any chance of recovery by one of the
following actions:
 o dying without any chance of recovery - well over a hundred ways to
do this.
 o leaving the dungeon when you DO NOT have the Amulet of Yendor -
basically, you "escaped" instead of winning.
 o sacrificing the Amulet of Yendor on the wrong Altar on the Astral
Plane - you finished in "celestial disgrace".
 o converting your alignment permanently before entering the quest.

All but the last cause ends the game as well. You can continue to play
after a permanent alignment conversion but will not be able to retrieve
the Bell of Opening. To explain the last one, you will permanently
convert yourself ONLY if you
 o try to convert an altar when your alignment is negative, or
 o if you sacrifice a unicorn of your own alignment on another god's
altar.

